editorialMd:
Build removalOrder

Put all numbers from `readings` into a min-heap. A min-heap is a tree-shaped collection that keeps its smallest number at the top. Remove the smallest number, record it, and repeat until the heap is empty. Keep repeated numbers. `removalOrder` is the removal order.

Return the answer

Multiply each number in `removalOrder` by its position, counting from 1: the first number by 1, the second by 2, and so on. Add those products. Store the sum in `weightedTotal`. Complete `priorityBasketBossReceipt` so it returns `weightedTotal`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `removalOrder` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n log n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

javascript
function priorityBasketBossReceipt(readings) {
  const a=readings; let out=[];
  const heap=[];for(const x of a){heap.push(x);let i=heap.length-1;while(i){const p=(i-1)>>1;if(heap[p]<=heap[i])break;[heap[p],heap[i]]=[heap[i],heap[p]];i=p;}}while(heap.length){out.push(heap[0]);const last=heap.pop();if(!heap.length)break;heap[0]=last;let i=0;while(true){let j=i,l=2*i+1,r=l+1;if(l<heap.length&&heap[l]<heap[j])j=l;if(r<heap.length&&heap[r]<heap[j])j=r;if(j===i)break;[heap[i],heap[j]]=[heap[j],heap[i]];i=j;}}
  return out.reduce((s,x,i)=>s+(i+1)*x,0);
}


